    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98-a3">

                <pb facs="0270" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg142"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Meeks and
                            Garley to Mr. Beattie</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Custom-House, New York City</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Surveyor’s Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 30,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We have to report that the steamship City
                    of Mexico is now almost laden.</p>
                <p>Her cargo consists of a miscellaneous lot of goods, such as is generally exported
                    to Mexico and South American ports, viz: hardware, glass, dry goods, lard,
                    machinery, &amp;c.; also seven cases cartridges and ten kegs shot.</p>
                <p>By the most careful inspection of each package laden, we find nothing in her
                    cargo or equipments that would violate sections 5283, 5286, or 5287, R. S.</p>
                <p>Respectfully submitted.</p>
                <closer><signed>MEEKS AND GARLEY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Inspectors.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
